      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-142871: multiplying out gives cos²x−sin²x=1−2sin²x. q-127841, q-1400, and q-127846: the cross product is |a||b|sin(θ)n, giving 15n, approximately 28.9254n rounded to 29n, and approximately 28.9254n rounded to 28.9n, respectively. q-146313 and q-146263: parallel vectors have zero cross product. q-123203: cos(5π/3)=1/2 and sin²(5π/3)=3/4, giving ⟨3,3/4⟩. q-50083: substitution gives ⟨2²,3·2³⟩=⟨4,24⟩. q-161507: substitution gives the column vector with entries ln(1)=0, 25, and −9. q-74997: r(3)=⟨8,6⟩ has magnitude √(64+36)=10. q-23602: replacing 1+cot²θ with csc²θ reduces the expression to cosθ. q-119904: cos²z·csc²z=cot²z. q-23849: cot²x/csc²x=cos²x, so the expression is zero. q-65518: writing the expression as cos²θ/(1−sinθ) gives 1+sinθ. q-23898: tan²θ(csc²θ−1)=tan²θ·cot²θ=1. q-23897: factoring csc²θ gives csc²θ(1+cot²θ)=csc⁴θ. Trigonometric equalities hold on each original expression's domain. No prior submissions or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
